2026-08-03; design doc § anchor + plan §5 1b); the ballot-build reuses the precomputed saturation
result rather than re-invoking. In review; not pushed."

## Open questions / follow-ups
- None blocking. The opt-in choice leaves a forward-looking footgun for when multi-analyzer ships
  (an operator adding a second analyzer must also list saturation to keep its vote) — the dev-guide (§8)
  documents this, and it is flagged to revisit at PR-2 (`ta-anchor-dynamic-refresh-plan.md`), where
  both-enabled becomes real.
